# Velora Project Roadmap & Actionable TODOs

> **Generated from comprehensive line-by-line audit.**  
> Priority scale: `[P0] Critical / Security` > `[P1] Architecture & Core Flow` > `[P2] Commercial Feature Gaps` > `[P3] DX & Infrastructure`

---

## 🔴 Phase 1: Security & Critical Vulnerabilities [P0]

- [ ] **Fix Broken Object-Level Authorization (BOLA/IDOR) on Products**
  - **Issue:** Any seller can modify or delete any product on the platform or create listings under another seller's store.
  - **Files:**
    - [`ProductController.js`](file:///c:/Users/Omid/X/Code/Velora/Backend/controller/ProductController.js#L31-L61)
    - [`ProductService.js`](file:///c:/Users/Omid/X/Code/Velora/Backend/services/ProductService.js#L57-L126)
  - **Action:**
    - In `createProduct`: Validate that `req.body.storeId` is owned by `req.user.id` (`ownerOfStore`).
    - In `patchProductByid`: Pass `req.user.id` and ensure the target product's store belongs to the requesting seller.
    - In `deleteProductById`: Query both `_id: productId` and verify store ownership before soft deleting.

- [ ] **Prevent Privilege Escalation on Order Status**
  - **Issue:** Any authenticated customer can submit `PATCH /server/checkout/order/:id` with `{ "orderStatus": "delivered" }` to mark their own orders delivered or shipped.
  - **Files:**
    - [`Patch_checkout.js`](file:///c:/Users/Omid/X/Code/Velora/Backend/routes/versionOne/checkout/Patch_checkout.js#L12-L18)
    - [`OrderController.js`](file:///c:/Users/Omid/X/Code/Velora/Backend/controller/OrderController.js#L42-L53)
  - **Action:**
    - Restrict customer status updates strictly to `"cancelled"` (and only when payment/order is still pending).
    - Status transitions like `"shipped"` and `"delivered"` must require seller or admin credentials.

- [ ] **Inject `role: "customer"` into Customer JWT & Restore `requireCustomer`**
  - **Issue:** Customer login issues tokens without `role: "customer"`, causing [`requireCustomer`](file:///c:/Users/Omid/X/Code/Velora/Backend/middleware/auth/system/Customer.js) to fail and forcing routes to disable role checks.
  - **Files:**
    - [`CustomerService.js`](file:///c:/Users/Omid/X/Code/Velora/Backend/services/CustomerService.js#L152-L165)
    - [`Post_reviews.js`](file:///c:/Users/Omid/X/Code/Velora/Backend/routes/versionOne/reviews/Post_reviews.js#L4-L16)
  - **Action:**
    - Add `role: 'customer'` to JWT signing payload in `CustomerService.loginCustomer`.
    - Un-comment and restore `requireCustomer` guard in `Post_reviews.js` and other customer-only endpoints.

- [ ] **Fix Ghost Model Reference (`ref: "User"`)**
  - **Issue:** `Order.js` and `Cart.js` set `ref: "User"`, but no `User` model exists (models are `Customer` and `storeOwner`). Calling `.populate("userId")` causes a fatal `MissingSchemaError`.
  - **Files:**
    - [`Order.js`](file:///c:/Users/Omid/X/Code/Velora/Backend/model/Order.js#L59)
    - [`Cart.js`](file:///c:/Users/Omid/X/Code/Velora/Backend/model/Cart.js#L74)
  - **Action:**
    - Update `ref: "User"` to `ref: "Customer"`.

- [ ] **Fix Soft-Delete Accounting in BaseService Pagination**
  - **Issue:** `countDocuments(filter)` counts soft-deleted documents, returning inaccurate page and total counts.
  - **Files:**
    - [`BaseService/index.js`](file:///c:/Users/Omid/X/Code/Velora/Backend/services/BaseService/index.js#L45-L57)
  - **Action:**
    - Change `this.model.countDocuments(filter)` to `this.model.countDocuments(activeFilter)`.

- [ ] **Prevent Account Enumeration on Registration**
  - **Issue:** `POST /customers/register` returns `201 Created` with full user profile when an email already exists.
  - **Files:**
    - [`CustomerService.js`](file:///c:/Users/Omid/X/Code/Velora/Backend/services/CustomerService.js#L61-L71)
  - **Action:**
    - Return a generic response or throw a standardized 409 error without leaking user ID or verification status.

- [ ] **Remove Hardcoded DNS in Server Bootstrap**
  - **Issue:** `dns.setServers(["1.1.1.1", "8.8.8.8"])` breaks containerized/private cloud networking.
  - **Files:**
    - [`Server.js`](file:///c:/Users/Omid/X/Code/Velora/Backend/Server.js#L18-L20)
  - **Action:**
    - Remove hardcoded DNS override or gate behind an explicit dev environment flag.

